ve is that Candidate\u202fA:\n* **Anticipates dangerous situations** and can see complex connections, which suggests strong situational awareness and technical insight.\n* **Has very good leadership qualities** and excellent spatial vision, both valuable for long\u2011distance operations.\n* **Can be unorganized** and **is sometimes not good at taking criticism**, indicating a potential weakness in consistently following procedures and in responding constructively to feedback.\nBecause of the latter points, if crew members perceive him as a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d or as someone who is not open to new ideas, it could undermine **crew cooperation**. Reluctance to accept criticism or new input can create friction in the cockpit, reduce the willingness of others to share information, and make it harder to maintain a collaborative, safety\u2011focused environment."}
